ars began to _______ down her cheeks.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>trickle<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>trickle<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>trickle<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: trickle down \/ trickle in \/ a trickle of \/ slow trickle<\/span><\/p><p>similar: drip \/ dribble \/ seep \/ ooze<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: gush \/ pour \/ flood<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"trickle","study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":3,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":2,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-06","reviewed_on":"2026-06-16","due_at":"2026-06-19T08:13:22+00:00","previous_state":{"state":"review","due_at":"2026-06-15T15:09:26+00:00","interval":1,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":1,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-06","reviewed_on":"2026-06-14"}},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"4 nap","good":"8 nap","easy":"10 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-06-19T08:08:54+00:00"},{"id":51416,"front":"<p>The company decided to _______ a major new construction project, despite the economic uncertainty. <em>(elv\u00e1llal \/ belekezd)<\/em><\/p><p>He had to _______ a long and difficult journey to reach his destination. <em>(megtesz \/ v\u00e9grehajt)<\/em><\/p><p>The government will _______ a thorough investigation into the allegations of corruption. <em>(ind\u00edt \/ foganatos\u00edt)<\/em><\/p><p>Are you willing to _______ the responsibility for this decision? <em>(mag\u00e1ra v\u00e1llal \/ felv\u00e1llal)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">elv\u00e1llal \/ megtesz \/ belekezd<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): elutas\u00edt \/ visszautas\u00edt \/ lemond<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a project = projektet elv\u00e1llal (pl. They will _______ a new research project next month.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a task = feladatot elv\u00e1llal\/v\u00e9grehajt (pl. It&#039;s a difficult task, but someone has to _______ it.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a journey = utat megtesz (pl. Explorers often _______ perilous journeys.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a responsibility = felel\u0151ss\u00e9get felv\u00e1llal (pl. He was reluctant to _______ such a huge responsibility.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ an investigation = vizsg\u00e1latot ind\u00edt\/lefolytat (pl. The police decided to _______ an immediate investigation.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>undertake<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>undertaking<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>undertake<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: undertake a project \/ undertake a task \/ undertake a journey \/ undertake responsibility<\/span><\/p><p>similar: commence \/ embark on \/ perform \/ assume<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: abandon \/ forego \/ decline<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"undertake","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":3,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":2,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-06","reviewed_on":"2026-06-16","due_at":"2026-06-19T08:15:35+00:00","previous_state":{"state":"review","due_at":"2026-06-15T15:08:53+00:00","interval":1,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":1,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-06","reviewed_on":"2026-06-14"}},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"4 nap","good":"8 nap","easy":"10 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-06-19T08:10:49+00:00"},{"id":51438,"front":"<p>It was a _______ coincidence that we met at the airport; we hadn&#039;t planned it. <em>(puszta \/ v\u00e9letlen)<\/em><\/p><p>The _______ fact that he was present doesn&#039;t prove his guilt. <em>(csup\u00e1n \/ egyszer\u0171en)<\/em><\/p><p>Despite the elaborate packaging, the product itself was a _______ disappointment. <em>(tiszta \/ teljes)<\/em><\/p><p>He dismissed her concerns as _______ sentimentality, not real problems. <em>(csup\u00e1n \/ egyszer\u0171)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">puszta \/ csup\u00e1n \/ egyszer\u0171<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): jelent\u0151s \/ fontos \/ l\u00e9nyeges<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _______ coincidence = puszta v\u00e9letlen (pl. It was a _______ coincidence that we both wore red.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 the _______ fact = a puszta t\u00e9ny (pl. The _______ fact that he smiled doesn&#039;t mean he agreed.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ numbers = puszta sz\u00e1mok (pl. _______ numbers don&#039;t always tell the whole story.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _______ formality = puszta formalit\u00e1s (pl. Signing the document was a _______ formality.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>mere<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>mere<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>merely<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: mere existence \/ mere chance \/ mere words \/ mere suggestion<\/span><\/p><p>similar: only \/ simple \/ nothing more than \/ bare<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: significant \/ substantial \/ important<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"mere","study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":3,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":2,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-10","reviewed_on":"2026-06-16","due_at":"2026-06-19T08:10:46+00:00","previous_state":{"state":"review","due_at":"2026-06-15T15:19:08+00:00","interval":1,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":1,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-10","reviewed_on":"2026-06-14"}},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"4 nap","good":"8 nap","easy":"10 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-06-19T15:26:04+00:00"},{"id":51437,"front":"<p>The new design aims to _______ the company&#039;s commitment to sustainability. <em>(megtestes\u00edt \/ kifejez)<\/em><\/p><p>She truly seems to _______ the spirit of adventure, always seeking new challenges. <em>(megtestes\u00edt \/ k\u00e9pvisel)<\/em><\/p><p>In his later works, the artist began to _______ more abstract concepts. <em>(megtestes\u00edt \/ form\u00e1ba \u00f6nt)<\/em><\/p><p>The ancient ruins _______ the rich history of the civilization that once thrived there. <em>(tan\u00faskodik \/ mag\u00e1ban foglal)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">megtestes\u00edt \/ kifejez \/ mag\u00e1ban foglal<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): elhanyagol \/ mell\u0151z \/ tagad<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a principle = egy elvet megtestes\u00edt (pl. The new policy aims to embody a principle of fairness.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ the spirit of = valaminek a szellem\u00e9t megtestes\u00edti (pl. She truly embodies the spirit of generosity.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ an idea = egy \u00f6tletet megtestes\u00edt (pl. The sculpture was created to embody an idea of freedom.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ values = \u00e9rt\u00e9keket megtestes\u00edt (pl. The leader should embody the values of the community.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>embody<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>embodiment<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>embody<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: embody the spirit \/ embody a principle \/ embody an idea \/ embody values<\/span><\/p><p>similar: represent \/ manifest \/ personify \/ incarnate<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: disembody \/ neglect \/ exclude<\/span><